 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
 
-A compiled **upgrade distribution planner draft** is available as `UpgradeDistributionPlanner.Generate(input, seed, options)`. It returns a deterministic plan and achieved-distribution report, preserves the exact reward/type pool, pins metal detectors, targets 82–91% local truck-specific rewards and applies the first-region foreign preference only to shared upgrades. No-home truck-specific parts are distributed separately. Regional type mixes and percentages are soft goals. It performs no file writes and is not connected to the Upgrades UI yet; verified compatibility/composite tire IDs and effective truck/contract-reward homes must be supplied by a future catalog adapter. See [the planner draft and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
+A compiled **slot-based upgrade selection draft** is available as `UpgradeDistributionPlanner.Generate(input, seed, options)`. It selects new rewards from the supplied eligible full catalog while retaining each pickup's original type and fixed metal detectors. Truck-specific slots prefer unused upgrades compatible with local obtainable trucks; shared slots draw from all eligible shared parts of that type, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. There is no locality quota or whole-plan optimizer, and original reward IDs/counts need not be retained. It performs no file writes and is not connected to the Upgrades UI yet; verified compatibility/composite tire IDs and effective truck/contract-reward homes must be supplied by a future catalog adapter. See [the planner draft and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
 
 **Editors → Addons** provides a read-only addon/upgrade catalog using Cargo's main table, description and source-properties layout. Reload runs in the background. Shared column sorting/filtering covers names, type/category, IDs and ID scope, socket/component family, content, price, rank, exploration flag and map reward references. Selecting an item lists each level SSO's map, zone and reward index, plus XML properties and their source files. Explicit file parents are followed; templates remain visible source data without expansion, and full truck compatibility is not inferred. Tire names are local to their wheel family; unresolved map reward IDs remain clearly marked. This does not stage or edit game data. See [the upgrade investigation](upgrade-map-investigation.md) for the confirmed map-zone → level-settings → part-definition relationship and replacement limits.
 
